# Push chat edits

When a request in this repo changes files, finish the edit, then commit and push to `origin` `main` in the same turn. Do not ask first.

- Stage only files that belong to the request.
- Use a short commit message that says why the change exists.
- Push with `git push origin HEAD`. Never force-push.
- Skip the commit when there is nothing to commit.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
- If the commit or push fails, fix it and try once more, then say what blocked it.
